WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.883
Deception can have many goals,

00:00:01.883 --> 00:00:06.876
but from a defensive perspective the goals often cluster into a few useful categories.

00:00:06.876 --> 00:00:11.513
Some activity is meant to create urgency: act now, approve now, share now,

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.939
disable the control now.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:15.079
Some is meant to create confusion,

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:20.072
making the team spend time on the wrong claim or argue over incomplete context.

00:00:20.072 --> 00:00:25.065
Some is meant to hide source, intent, or responsibility, so that a request, artifact,

00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:27.918
or narrative appears more trustworthy than it is.

00:00:27.918 --> 00:00:29.701
Defensive signals are not proof.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.198
They are reasons to apply more care.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.051
Missing provenance, unusual urgency, unexplained gaps, selective screenshots,

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:35.764
conflicting timestamps,

00:00:35.764 --> 00:00:41.114
and pressure to bypass normal process should all change how an analyst handles the claim.

00:00:41.114 --> 00:00:43.967
A single indicator may have an innocent explanation.

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:47.890
A pattern of indicators may justify escalation, preservation, and independent corroboration.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.673
Selective evidence is especially important.

00:00:49.673 --> 00:00:51.813
A message thread can be cropped.

00:00:51.813 --> 00:00:55.023
A log line can be separated from surrounding events.

00:00:55.023 --> 00:00:56.806
A domain, file hash, username,

00:00:56.806 --> 00:01:01.799
or ticket number can be real while the conclusion attached to it is wrong.

00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:04.295
The analyst should ask what is missing,

00:01:04.295 --> 00:01:07.149
what system of record can confirm the artifact,

00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:12.855
and whether the presented evidence supports the exact claim or only a weaker version of it.

00:01:12.855 --> 00:01:17.491
The purpose of naming signals is not to make teams suspicious of everything.

00:01:17.491 --> 00:01:22.484
It is to give them a repeatable way to move from reaction to verification.

00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:26.051
When urgency is high, process becomes more valuable, not less.

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.190
Trusted channels, approval workflows, documented assumptions,

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:33.540
and clear escalation paths help teams make timely decisions without giving pressure the steering wheel.
